;;; `std.math.int` — a malformed numeral handed to a tagged call as a part:
;;; checked, flagged, dead.
;;;
;;; ── What the theory promises ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; An integer built from an invalid decimal is invalid (Q-M1f.404): a call
;;; asks `(int-check (int P N))` of the parts it is handed
;;; (`int-add-call-runs`), the integer's check asks `std.math.decimal`'s of
